  "market_context": "Bearish trend on NZD/USD 1-minute chart with multiple downside breaks of structure and no FVGs. Price recently broke lower, leaving a clean unmitigated gap and order block above the current structure.",
  "key_observation": "The break above the swing high was interpreted not as a valid CHoCH but as a liquidity grab targeting stops above the supply zone formed by the order block and FVG.",
  "analysis_steps": [
    "Step 1: Identified a moving downtrend on NZD/USD 1-minute with multiple BOS to the downside and no FVGs in the recent structure.",
    "Step 2: Spotted a clean unmitigated fair value gap and order block on the left side of the chart, above the current price and swing high.",
    "Step 3: Recognized that the price breaking above the swing high was a liquidity grab (not a valid CHoCH) because it targeted the supply zone where stop-losses and pending orders were clustered.",
    "Step 4: Decided to place a sell limit order just below the order block (supply zone), with stop-loss above the order block and target at the next HTF level.",
    "Step 5: Applied standard risk management: break even at 2× risk by closing half position, and used HTF structure for target placement."
  ],
  "outcome": null,
  "lessons": "In a strong downtrend, a break above a swing high into an unmitigated order block/FVG zone is likely a liquidity grab—not a reversal. Trade the retest of the supply zone with confluence of OB and FVG.",
